{ "kind": "label", "bind": "operation" }
{ "kind": "status_pill", "bind": "status" }
{ "kind": "label", "bind": "occurred_at" }
```

**One element per line.** Each is a singular, atomic unit. The spec is flat — each line is one component binding one value. The LLM doesn't write nested trees, it writes a flat list where each line is `{ kind, bind }` — one element, one datum, one line.

That's the formatting tip: the DSL elements in the `children` array are each a single self-contained line. The LLM composes by listing atomic bindings linearly. The `stack` is just layout grouping; the real units are the individual `{ "kind": "...", "bind": "..." }` entries.

