AI Overview
To render only one element from a json-render specification containing multiple elements, change the root property in your spec object to point exclusively to the ID of the target element you want to display, leaving the unselected elements out of the root's tree or children array. 
How to Isolate a Single Element
Change the root pointer: Set root to point directly to the key of the specific element you want to render.
Remove child links: Ensure the targeted element does not include the other elements inside its children array.
Filter the elements map: Pass only the required element (and any nested dependencies it needs) inside the elements dictionary. 
